{"date":"2026-02-10T19:01:23.252Z","editing":{},"event":"chat","feedback":{},"folding":[],"history":[{"author_id":"fba1174b-3740-4f98-9a32-6f1b77896af2","content":"<span class=\"user-mention\" account-id=google-gemini-3-flash-preview-16k >@Gemini 3 Flash</span> Please give me a hint to help me fix my code. Do not provide the complete solution - just point me in the right direction.\n\n<details open><summary>Context</summary>\n\nI ran a cell in a Jupyter notebook.\n\nI received the following error:\n\n```python\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRecursionError                            Traceback (most recent call last)\nCell In[127], line 67\n     64         full_com = \" \".join([intro, attributes(stdnt), key_grdes(stdnt), outcome_(stdnt), final_grade(stdnt)])\n     65         print(\"\\n\" + fullcoms + \"\\n\")\n---> 67 put_it_together()\n\nCell In[127], line 64, in put_it_together(file_name)\n     60 for studs in stdnt:\n     62     intro = f\"this semester in {stdnt[1]}, we have continued building on the foundations of speaking, listening, reading, and writing in Mandarin. Students practiced more complex sentence strutures, expanded their vocabulary, and explored culteral topics through conversations, tests, and projects.\"\n---> 64     full_com = \" \".join([intro, attributes(stdnt), key_grdes(stdnt), outcome_(stdnt), final_grade(stdnt)])\n     65     print(\"\\n\" + fullcoms + \"\\n\")\n\nCell In[127], line 6, in attributes(stdnt)\n      1 def attributes(stdnt):\n      2     \"\"\"\n      3     Takes in the attributes of the student,\n      4     returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n      5     \"\"\"\n----> 6     parts_new = attributes(stdnt).split(\", \")\n      7     adj1 = parts_new[0]\n      8     adj2 = parts_new[1]\n\nCell In[127], line 6, in attributes(stdnt)\n      1 def attributes(stdnt):\n      2     \"\"\"\n      3     Takes in the attributes of the student,\n      4     returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n      5     \"\"\"\n----> 6     parts_new = attributes(stdnt).split(\", \")\n      7     adj1 = parts_new[0]\n      8     adj2 = parts_new[1]\n\n    [... skipping similar frames: attributes at line 6 (2969 times)]\n\nCell In[127], line 6, in attributes(stdnt)\n      1 def attributes(stdnt):\n      2     \"\"\"\n      3     Takes in the attributes of the student,\n      4     returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n      5     \"\"\"\n----> 6     parts_new = attributes(stdnt).split(\", \")\n      7     adj1 = parts_new[0]\n      8     adj2 = parts_new[1]\n\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n```\n\nMy Jupyter notebook using the Python 3 (Anaconda 2022) kernel contains:\n\n```python\ndef attributes(stdnt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes in the attributes of the student,\n    returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n    \"\"\"\n    parts_new = attributes(stdnt).split(\", \")\n    adj1 = parts_new[0]\n    adj2 = parts_new[1]\n    return f\"{stdnt[0]}, you are {adj1} and {adj2}. You are a joy to have in class, and I hope to keep hearing your ideas.\"\n        \n    for notes in all_adjs:\n        print(notes)\n    \ndef key_grades(stdnt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes in the overall performance and the final exam grade of the student,\n    returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n    \"\"\"\n   \n    sections_new = stdnt[3].split(\": \")\n    overall = sections_new[0]\n    final = sections_new[1]\n    grade_num = final.split(\"%\")\n    is_it_a_ninty = grade_num[0]\n    if is_it_a_ninty[0] == \"9\" or is_it_a_ninty[0:2] == \"10\":\n        return f\"Throughout the semester, you recieved {overall}, and finished the year with a {final}.\"\n           \n    else:\n        return f\"Throughout the semester, you recieved {overall}, and finished the year with an {final}.\"\n\n    \ndef outcome_recs(stdnt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes in the areas of improvement for the student,\n    returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n    \"\"\"\n    outcome = stdnt[4]\n    suggest = stdnt[5]\n    return (f\"For your area of growth, I suggest that we work on your {outcome}. To improve in this section, you should {suggest}.\")\n\ndef final_grade(stdnt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes in the final letter grade of the student,\n    returning a sentence with the information incorperated. \n    \"\"\"\n\n    gradde = stdnt[6]\n\n    if \"A\" in gradde:\n        grades.append(f\"Overall, you will recieved an {gradde}. Strong work this year. Keep it up!\")\n    elif \"B\" in gradde:\n        grades.append(f\"Overall, you will recieved an {gradde}. Strong work this year, let's keep pushing forward and please come to me with any questions.\")\n    else:\n        grades.append(f\"Overall, you will recieved an {gradde}. Good job so far, I really enoy your presence in this class.\")\n  \n\n\ndef put_it_together(file_name=\"teacher.csv\"):\n    stdnt = read_csv(file_name)\n    for studs in stdnt:\n        \n        intro = f\"this semester in {stdnt[1]}, we have continued building on the foundations of speaking, listening, reading, and writing in Mandarin. Students practiced more complex sentence strutures, expanded their vocabulary, and explored culteral topics through conversations, tests, and projects.\"\n\n        full_com = \" \".join([intro, attributes(stdnt), key_grdes(stdnt), outcome_(stdnt), final_grade(stdnt)])\n        print(\"\\n\" + fullcoms + \"\\n\")\n\nput_it_together()\n```\n\n</details>","date":"2026-02-10T19:01:23.252Z"}],"read-fba1174b-3740-4f98-9a32-6f1b77896af2":2,"sender_id":"fba1174b-3740-4f98-9a32-6f1b77896af2"}
{"date":"2026-02-10T19:01:23.255Z","editing":{},"event":"chat","generating":false,"history":[{"author_id":"google-gemini-3-flash-preview-16k","content":"The `RecursionError` occurs because, inside your `attributes(stdnt)` function, you are calling `attributes(stdnt)` again on line 6. This creates an infinite loop where the function keeps calling itself until Python hits its safety limit.\n\n**Hint:** Look at how you accessed data in your other functions. For example, in `key_grades(stdnt)`, you used `stdnt[3]`. In `attributes(stdnt)`, you likely meant to split a specific piece of data from the `stdnt` list/tuple rather than calling the function itself.","date":"2026-02-10T19:01:28.002Z"}],"reply_to":"2026-02-10T19:01:23.252Z","sender_id":"google-gemini-3-flash-preview-16k"}
